Hi,<br><br>The URDF file modelling our robot contains 333 links (output of getNumLinks) and thus the robot state won't compute due to: <br><a href="https://github.com/bulletphysics/bullet3/blob/34eb3d19bf4ec9c5faf6906b6a9d1f3cdf663441/examples/SharedMemory/PhysicsServerCommandProcessor.cpp#L7093" class="postlink">https://github.com/bulletphysics/bullet ... .cpp#L7093</a><br><br>Locally I am able to change the value of MAX_DEGREE_OF_FREEDOM and it seems to work well in our case but I'd like to know if there is any better way to make it work ? or any known workaround ?<br><br>regards<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=13574">XavierB</a> — Mon Mar 23, 2020 5:38 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
